  "answer_text": "# \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\udde6 Ukraine \u2014 Latest News (June 2026)\n\nHere is a summary of the latest developments regarding Ukraine and the ongoing war with Russia:\n\n---\n\n## \u2694\ufe0f Battlefield Situation\n\nUkraine's ability to impede the flow of Russian supplies and personnel to the front lines has grown in recent days, from the southern regions of Zaporizhia and Kherson to the eastern front, forcing the Russian army to a standstill, according to battlefield analysis.\n\nRussia's performance since December shows it can contest territory but cannot hold it, according to battlefield observers.\n\nGeneral Oleksandr Komarenko, head of the Main Operative Department at the General Staff of the Ukrainian Armed Forces, claimed that Ukrainian forces had restored control over 285.6 km\u00b2 in the Oleksandrivka direction. In total, Ukrainian forces had cleared 400 km\u00b2 of territory since the beginning of counteroffensive operations, and February 2026 became the **first month since 2024** when Ukraine regained more territory than it lost.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 Missile & Drone Strikes\n\nOn June 2, Russia fired a combination of 656 drones and 73 missiles into Ukrainian civilian areas, killing **23 people** and injuring at least 130. Ukraine intercepted 91.7% of the drones and 90.6% of the cruise missiles, but only **27%** of the ballistic missiles.\n\nRussia produces **120 ballistic missiles a month**, Zelenskyy told the Ukraine-NATO Council \u2014 twice as many as the Patriot interceptors the United States produces.\n\nMeanwhile, Ukraine has continued to strike refineries and munitions factories deep inside Russia, weakening its war effort.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Ukraine's Long-Range Capabilities\n\nOn May 31, Ukraine's 3rd Army Corps declared it had established fire control over the cities of Luhansk, Starobilsk, Alchevsk, Bryanka, and Kadiivka \u2014 all 50 to 90 km inside occupied Luhansk \u2014 and could strike targets at the Russian border, 205 km away. It was the **first time** Ukraine declared such interdiction power over the eastern region.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f Political Developments\n\nSensing the growing strength of their position, Ukrainian forces struck the city of **St. Petersburg** as Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived there for a high-profile economic forum, and President Zelenskyy wrote him an open letter telling him he could not win the war.\n\nKyrylo Budanov, head of military intelligence (HUR), was appointed to replace Andriy Yermak as head of the **Office of the President of Ukraine**.\n\n---\n\nWould you like more details on any specific aspect of the situation in Ukraine? \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\udde6",
